counter_convention:
ewtheorem{thm}[subsection]{Theorem} with thm-tweak/cor/cor-tweak/lemma/lemma-tweak/prop/rem/rem-tweak/defn-tweak/eg-tweak all sharing the 	exttt{subsection} counter (lines 199-224), so every numbered statement advances the subsection number and a following \subsection jumps past it (e.g. Lemma 2.2 sits inside 2.1 and the next heading is 2.3); 
ewtheorem{claim}[equation]{Claim} puts Claim on the equation counter, which 
umberwithin{equation}{subsection} (line 1192) makes subsubsection-local from section 4 onward, hence Claim 2.1 but Claim 4.8.5 and A.2.1; 
ewtheorem*{egs}{Examples} is unnumbered and the author device  egs/\egi/\eegs (lines 167-169) prints unnumbered "Examples (2.7)"-style items while advancing the subsection counter by hand with \addtocounter; the appendix re-uses its own A.n sequence because \section*{Appendix...} (2336) is followed by efstepcounter{section} (2338). Verified by simulation: 71/71 numbered positions reproduce their printed numbers under this convention.
